Grant private-project access from the member form (1.11.0)

The private_access column existed and the visibility rule read it, but
nothing could set it — so in practice only the owner ever saw a private
project. Third instance today of a column the app reads and no form
writes, after is_closed and is_review.

Only someone who has private access can grant it. Without that, a staff
admin holding members.manage could grant it to others, or to themselves
by editing their own record — a privilege escalation through the people
form. An absent value means "leave it alone" rather than "switch it off",
so a form without the field cannot silently revoke a grant.

